-- I28 (#2188) S2-DECL (d) bullet 2 -- TWO admitted declarations that AGREE.
-- The module graph is the recovered #1664 corpus VERBATIM (amodI/zmodI/fmodI copied from
-- `git show 23472016^:test/must_fail_fixtures/1664-decl-agreeing-both-admitted/`, the pin
-- that was drained and deleted 2026-08-29); this entry is that fixture's own `main.mdk`
-- with its #1664-specific header replaced.
--
-- Both `IA` and `IZ` are admitted (each is named in its OWN import clause, so S1-NS (a)'s
-- TYPE arm admits both), and both denote the SAME thing:
--   * `IA.mth : a -> Int -> Int` dispatches at argument 0, head String -- and amodI
--     declares NO `impl IA String`, so IA falls to the imported standalone.
--   * `IZ.mth : Int -> b -> Int` dispatches at argument 1, head Int -- and no
--     `impl IZ Int` exists anywhere, so IZ falls to the imported standalone too.
-- Two admitted, one denotation => (d) bullet 2, ACCEPT, and the denotation is
-- `fmodI.mth = 99`. VALUE HAND-DERIVED from the declared signatures, and independently
-- derived first-hand by the deleted pin's own claim.txt before this fixture existed.
--
-- ⚠️ `impl IZ String` IS IN THE GRAPH and must stay: its body returns 7, which is
-- NEITHER declaration's denotation here. A 7 on any verb is the S2-DECL (c) violation
-- #1664 pinned (an impl answering a query it was never asked), not a value drift.
-- `fmodI.mth` is the load-bearing standalone shadow -- without it `mth` is not a shadow
-- at all and none of this machinery is reached.
--
-- The order-swapped companion pins S2-DECL (e): this cell must not move when the two
-- interface import clauses are swapped.
import fmodI.{mth}
import amodI.{IA, af}
import zmodI.{IZ, zf}

main = println (mth "abc" 5 + af 0 + zf 0)
